<article class="env-lemma" id="0BRC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BRC">Lemma <span data-tag="0BRC">10.46.9</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\varphi $ is integral, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\varphi $ induces an injective map of spectra, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\varphi $ induces purely inseparable residue field extensions. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $\varphi $ induces a homeomorphism from $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S)$ onto a closed subset of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ and for any ring map $R \to R'$ properties (1), (2), (3) are true for $R' \to R' \otimes _ R S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The map on spectra is closed by Lemmas <a href="/tag/00HZ" data-tag="00HZ">10.41.6</a> and <a href="/tag/00GU" data-tag="00GU">10.36.22</a>. The properties are preserved under base change by Lemmas <a href="/tag/0BRB" data-tag="0BRB">10.46.8</a> and <a href="/tag/02JK" data-tag="02JK">10.36.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>